          "name": "Spiny Defense",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "As a move action, a boundfat can roll itself up into a spiny ball. While rolled up, it gains a +3 enhancement bonus to its existing natural armor, and any creature attempting to grapple the boundfat takes 1d6 damage on making a grapple check. While rolled up, a boundfat cannot take an action other than leaving this state or casting a spell. The boundfat can leave this state as a move action.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "This is a short and plump, vaguely reptilian-amphibian creature with bright yellow skin, a series of spikes on their back, and a mischievous grin."
